CORE PROBLEM TO SOLVE
==================================================

Real opportunities are messy because:
- titles are vague or bureaucratic
- eligibility is buried in prose
- purpose is often hidden in descriptions
- population, activity, and org-type cues are inconsistent
- fields vary by source
- some sources use jargon instead of plain mission terms

The current matcher works best when it receives clean structured signals such as:
- clear mission phrases
- normalized domains
- explicit applicant types
- explicit population tags
- explicit activity tags

This new layer must infer those signals from real data.

